WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.120
My supervisor asked me to do a presentation next week

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.090
I want to start preparing for it now

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.240
but I don’t know what to do

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.220
It depends on what your goal is

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.040
Is the purpose of your presentation to inform

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.000
train or sell?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.090
I think it’s to report on 

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.000
the new sales campaign for our product

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.120
So my goal of this presentation is to keep everyone

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:30.020
updated on the progress of this campaign

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.030
Great

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.160
So do you know who will be at the presentation? 

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.140
Who is your target audience? 

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.220
You should analyze and understand your audience.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.000 
What are their work backgrounds, 

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.260
age range and awareness of your topic?

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.130
I am speaking to a group of senior sales representatives

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.110 
who are very experienced 

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.200
and familiar with our product already

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.110
They are quite different from newbies

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.200 
I don’t need to spend time explaining the product 

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.220
or sales strategies to them, right?

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.080
Correct. Since you know your goal and your audience already

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.280
you can start setting the objectives for your presentation

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.130
What is the difference between a goal and an objective?

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.090
A goal is the general accomplishment 

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.080
you aim to reach after the presentation

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:25.050 
In your case, your goal is to let the participants 

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.230
be aware of the recent sales campaign

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.100 
Objectives are similar to goals but slightly different

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.110 
Have you heard of a “SMART” objective?    

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.000
Oh yes, it has become very popular

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.280 
The S in SMART means specific

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.150
the M means measurable

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.250
the A is for attainable

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.080 
R is for relevant and T means time-based

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.080
Right

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Those are the five criteria a good objective should have

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.200 
For example 

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.200
what do you expect the audience to accomplish 

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.100
after the presentation? 

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.150
Set a deadline or a measure method

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.150
to evaluate their achievement 

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:15.110
Let me try to set my objectives as follows

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.230 
After this presentation, the audience should be able to

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.210 
1. list three major activities of the campaign

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:31.070 
2. talk about the good and the bad of these events so far

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.260 
and 3. evaluate the effectiveness of this campaign

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.260
and give feedback by the end of this month 

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.130
That sounds good

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:47.200
You now have very “smart” objectives for your presentation


